    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25230" root="صوف" body-key="S">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صُوفَانَةٌ</span></b> , applied to a ewe, is fem. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صُوفَانٌ</span>:
see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَافٌ</span>. (AHeyth, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also <i>A certain
herb,</i> or <i>leguminous plant,</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَقْلَةٌ</span>,) <i>downy,</i> (M,
K,) <i>and short,</i> (K,) mentioned by Aboo-Nasr as
<i>of the kind termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَحْرَار</span> [pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُرٌّ</span>], but not
specifically described by him. (AHn, M.)

